\section[Stage 131]{Stage 131: Parent Micro-Threshold for Canonical Mouth Compensation}
\label{stage:131}

\stagefield{Part / anchor}{Part IV; primary anchor \resultanchor{MTDC-T8}.}
\claimstatus{\StatusExactClosure{}.}

\stagefield{Purpose}{Stage~131 is a positive mouth-source and boundary layer ledger step.  Its audit target is the verification output quoted below.}

\stagefield{Inputs}{This stage imports the lower compensated core branch, positivity of the local mouth source, and the explicit GNLS/localized-Maxwell boundary-layer reduction.  It does not change the parent action or the grouped-lane ontology; it works inside the declared reduced branch and tests the next algebraic or realization condition.}

\stagefield{Verification}{SymPy audit: \StageFile{scripts/moving_throat_pde_stage131_parent_mouth_threshold_sympy_audit.py}; transcript: \StageFile{scripts/output/moving_throat_pde_stage131_parent_mouth_threshold_sympy_audit.txt}.  Mathematica audit: \StageFile{mathematica/moving_throat_pde_stage131_parent_mouth_threshold_mathematica_audit.wl}; transcript: \StageFile{mathematica/output/moving_throat_pde_stage131_parent_mouth_threshold_mathematica_audit.txt}.}

\stagefield{Derivation ledger}{The verification step belongs to the \emph{Positive mouth-source and boundary layer} block.  The computation isolates the positive source families, mouth-bias map, and micro-threshold for canonical compensation.}

\begin{quote}
Canonical branch is the parent threshold \(T_m-q_*A'_0=\Pi_*\Theta_\sigma/L\).
